INT. DRAGON'S TAX OFFICE - DAY

A cave lined with ledgers. Gold coins in neat stacks. A huge brass desk, a quill taller than a man.

GORLAN THRUM (40s, goblin accountant, ink-stained, eyeshade) sits on a towering stool. PHINEAS ABERNATHY-OLU (30s, human farmer, hat in hands) stands before him, shaking.

GORLAN
Your tithe is eleven sheep.

PHINEAS
Eleven, Master Gorlan?

GORLAN
Eleven.

PHINEAS
I have nine.

GORLAN
You have nine and a ewe in lamb.

PHINEAS
She isn't due until spring.

GORLAN
Lambs count.

A rumble shakes the cave. Dust sifts from the ceiling. A voice booms from somewhere beyond the ledgers.

VESUVIA (O.S.)
Gorlan, is the farmer negotiating?

GORLAN
(calling back)
No, Your Radiance.

PHINEAS
(muttering)
I would never.

VESUVIA (O.S.)
Good. I dislike negotiation.

GORLAN
Phineas, the dragon is generous but not patient. Choose.

PHINEAS
What are my choices?

GORLAN
Eleven sheep, or an apple pie every Sunday for ten years.

PHINEAS
Pie?

GORLAN
Her Radiance has a sweet tooth.

PHINEAS
Then I choose the pie.

VESUVIA (O.S.)
(delighted)
Excellent.
